{"title":"TOPHATs Nuit Blanche, a Blue Moon and a Beer Landing","startsAt":"2026-10-03T19:00:00-04:00","endsAt":"2026-10-03T22:30:00-04:00","status":"ACTIVE","type":"PHYSICAL","description":"Join Lawrence, your top hatted host, for an evening of Nuit Blanche art and Hops and Happy Hour treats.\n\nTemperature are to be around 10 C, so layer up as it will be cooler by the lake.\n\nWe will meet-up at Blue Moon Brewery at 7 pm for a refreshing Belgian brew.\n\nhttps://www.bluemooncanada.ca/en-CA/beers\n3 Tecumseth St\n\nAt 7:30 pmish, we will begin our Nuit Blanche adventure visiting the two exhibits in the STACKT Market\n\n“Magnetic Mother” by Micki-Lee Smith, Zakriya Bashir-Hill , Pratap Mathews #30\nRemember \\| Imagine by Hajar Moradi \\#29\n\nThen we will cross the Bathurst Street bridge, where you can get a scenic shot of our downtown as we head towards the lake.\n\nThe Bentway - Social Fabric: A Community Textile Activation by SHEEEP: Reza Nik, Sam Cruxton, Jocelyn Hernandez #64\n\nfollowed by The Bentway - A Persistent Crossing by Stanzie Tooth #65\n\nThen we will walk to Canoe Landing to see...\nKilim by Roda Medhat #53\nNight Waves by CityPlace and Fort York BIA\nFarsh by Roda Medhat #54\nGarrison Creek by Brian Leclerc #31\n\nAt 9 pmish is Happy Hour at Hunters Landing where we will rest, refresh before continuing on our adventure.\n\nhttps://www.thelandinggroup.ca/en/menu/hunters/happy-hour.html\n82 Fort York Blvd, Toronto, ON M5V 4A6\n\nBack down Bathurst to the lakeside to see\nOCAD University and the Delegation of the European Union to Canada - “The Light” and “Melting Temporalities” by Paul Murnaghan, Claire Brunet, Johnny Ranger #66\n\nThen over to one of my favourite summertime locations, the Toronto Music Garden to view.\nAscension by Ilene Sova #32\n\nWalking East along the waterfront we will arrive at The Grandmother Project by Peter Dillman #33\n\nSteps away is the Harbourfront Centre - Dance Stoops by Daily tous les jours #79\n\nOur final stop is at Love Park\nparol-parolan by HOT A!R ATEL!ER\n\nHere's the link to all the Nuit Blanche 2026 activities.\nhttps://www.toronto.ca/explore-enjoy/festivals-events/nuitblanche/all-art-projects/","venue":{"name":"clubhouse @ STACKT market","address":"28 Bathurst St, Toronto, ON M5V 0C6, Canada, Toronto","lat":43.64058,"lng":-79.40366,"city":"Toronto"},"fee":null,"group":"Toronto Beer Lovers","image":"https://secure.meetupstatic.com/photos/event/5/b/8/a/highres_536303434.jpeg"}